                "source": "Twitter for iPhone",
                "text": "Statement from Congressman Josh Brecheen Regarding Missed Vote\n\nDue to days of persistent flu-like symptoms, I notified House Leadership, including House Chief Deputy Whip Rep. Guy Reschenthaler, on Monday morning that I would likely have to miss votes this week. Throughout this period, I remained prepared to travel to Washington, D.C. should my presence be required for any critical votes.\n\nHouse leadership knew for a fact that today\u2019s partisan vote to impeach President Trump would not succeed. While I was absent for this vote solely due to health reasons, the official record will indicate that I would have voted to table this ridiculous motion. Had I been needed for this vote, I would have unequivocally voted to kill the impeachment measure.",
